     xmlns:swrlb="http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrlb#"
     xmlns:terms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:p-plan="http://purl.org/net/p-plan#"
     xmlns:schema="https://schema.org/"
     xmlns:supply_chain_model="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_figure8">
        <terms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-22</terms:created>
        <terms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8824-9577"/>
        <terms:description xml:lang="en">Self-contained Figure 8 collaboration plan plus one explicitly synthetic approved tender execution. Preserves the existing plan, schema, labels and transition inverses; restores the ten SWRL rules from the supplied intact supply-chain model. Six task Activities correspond to planned Steps, with actual-example participants, artifacts, outcomes and dated intervals. Demonstration data are not records of a real tender.</terms:description>
        <terms:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-05</terms:modified>
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.1080/00207543.2023.2242508"/>
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model"/>
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_figure8/sourceSchemaMetadata"/>
        <terms:title xml:lang="en">Collaborative tendering between a lead supplier and an invited partner</terms:title>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Figure 8: collaborative tendering plan</rdfs:label>
        <owl:versionInfo>figure8-plan-v1-2026-10-22</owl:versionInfo>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-10-22 — Changed by ChatGPT. Implemented Figure 8 as a separate planned collaboration on the updated supply-chain schema. Added placeholder organizations, contextual role instances, seven task definitions and planned assignments, five planned events, ten control-flow transitions, ten resource/message variables, four message exchanges, and one explicit exclusive choice with approval and rejection conditions. Preserved the figure&apos;s seven-task structure by documenting t11 as a send-and-await request/reply task. Retained separate initial-draft, contribution, revised tender and submitted-tender variables, and the single-producer P-Plan semantics. The submitted-tender slot is an explicit completion artifact chosen for this model. Preserved all ten existing SWRL rules. No runtime execution, branch-selection result, synthetic test data or inferred assertions are included.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-10-23 - Changed by ChatGPT. Corrected the inherited dcterms:created metadata value from 2025-28-11 to 2025-11-28 (interpreted as 28 November 2025) to address the reported AllegroGraph import error. Workflow definitions and rules are unchanged.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-11-05 (ChatGPT): Restored ten complete SWRL rules and variable declarations from supply_chain_model(1).ttl, removed damaged SWRL structures and structural annotation-property declarations, and added a synthetic approved execution with six StepExecutions, one enclosing run Activity, seven OWL-Time intervals, ten realized resource variables and qualified PROV associations/usages. Preserved prior plan assertions and inverse-property edits. No inferred assertions or SHACL constraints added.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-11-4 Changed by M. DeBellis. Several P-Plan properties had labels in CamelCase. I added skos:prefLabel values for them using my standard of all lower case for property labels. E.g., pplan:isStepOfPlan had label &quot;isStepOfPlan&quot;. I added a skos pref label: &quot;is step of plan&quot; and made it a lang string datatype.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">Control-flow transitions, message variables and decision conditions are explicit assertions. The existing SWRL rules infer candidate resource dependencies and shared inputs; they neither select a branch nor execute the plan. All declared steps and resource variables are explicitly distinct. Each produced variable has exactly one asserted producer. The call-for-tender variable is supplied externally.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">Figure 8 returns the partner vote to t11SendTenderForVotingTask. This model interprets that task as sending the voting request and awaiting the reply. Consequently t11 and t12 have resource dependencies in both directions; these describe a request/reply exchange, not a control-flow loop or a reason to assert each task precedes the other. An executable refinement may split sending and receiving into separate steps. The replacement branch ends where the figure ends; no retry loop is added.</skos:note>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">The paper and Figure 8 specify the task/lane topology and exchanges. Approval leading to submission and rejection leading to replacement are taken from the accompanying text. The figure does not name all message payloads or document slots, so their explicit names and version separation are modeling choices. LeadSupplier and InvitedPartner are placeholder organizations for the example, not identified real companies. No actual executions, messages, votes, tender documents or scenario timestamps are asserted. The inherited historical Time examples remain part of the self-contained base.</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


