    <!-- https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_figure8/sourceSchemaMetadata -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_figure8/sourceSchemaMetadata">
        <sulo:contains rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_figure8/sourceSchemaMetadata"/>
        <sulo:hasPart rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_figure8/sourceSchemaMetadata"/>
        <sulo:isIn rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_figure8/sourceSchemaMetadata"/>
        <sulo:isPartOf rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_figure8/sourceSchemaMetadata"/>
        <terms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-22</terms:created>
        <terms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8824-9577"/>
        <terms:description xml:lang="en">Self-contained experimental extension of the corrected process_model base, prepared for collaborative supply-chain tendering. Reuses P-Plan for planned steps and resource variables, PROV for actual executions and artifacts, and OWL-Time for dated intervals. Adds contextual role assignments, document versions, messages and explicit decision branches. Inspired by Figures 6 and 8 of Kazantsev et al. (2024).</terms:description>
        <terms:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-22</terms:modified>
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.1080/00207543.2023.2242508"/>
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/process_model"/>
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/baseModelMetadata"/>
        <terms:title xml:lang="en">Supply-chain collaboration: plans, resources and executions</terms:title>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Unchanged header annotations of the supply-chain schema used for this worked example.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Supply-chain collaboration model</rdfs:label>
        <owl:versionInfo>experimental-collaboration-v2-2026-10-22</owl:versionInfo>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-10-22 — Changed by ChatGPT. Added TaskStep, CommunicationStep, EventStep, StartEventStep and EndEventStep, plus eventForRole and triggeredByVariable, to support the start/end events and request/reply task shown in Figure 8. Made the six existing task categories subclasses of TaskStep. Declared TaskStep disjoint with EventStep and StartEventStep disjoint with EndEventStep. Preserved the ten existing SWRL rules, the underlying process-model vocabulary and all existing individuals. Kept Figure 8 instances in the separate self-contained supply_chain_figure8 ontology.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-10-22 — Changed by ChatGPT. Created a separate supply_chain_model ontology from the saved process_model base after synchronizing the later Bro_Pro hadRole and EmptyCollection/Collection repairs. Kept the base vocabulary definitions and all eight existing SWRL rules unchanged. Added a compact collaboration planning/execution vocabulary for step categories, planned roles, document version lineage, messages and decision conditions with explicit alternative transitions. Added two enabled SWRL rules for same-plan flow dependencies and shared input variables between explicitly distinct steps. The paper&apos;s shared-output rule and automatic conversion of dependencies to XOR were not adopted. Preserved the base header as sc:baseModelMetadata. No Figure 8 instances, synthetic tests or inferred assertions are included. The separate process_model.ttl file was not modified by this extension.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">The two added resource-dependency rules require distinct steps (owl:differentFrom or owl:AllDifferent) in the same explicitly identified plan. They infer candidate resource links, not execution order, resource contention, exclusive choices or authorization to execute a step. An ExclusiveChoice groups ConditionalTransition alternatives whose DecisionCondition records a decision variable and expected outcome. A workflow controller or human evaluates those conditions and selects the branch; OWL/SWRL here does not enforce executable XOR behavior. No closed-world completeness validation is supplied.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">Use distinct p-plan:Variable individuals for distinct planned document versions and contributions. p-plan:isOutputVarOf is functional, so one output variable must not be assigned to two explicitly different producing steps. Actual artifacts are p-plan:Entity instances linked through correspondsToVariable; that mapping is also functional in the retained P-Plan ontology.</skos:note>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Reusable schema for collaboration plans and their executions. Worked scenario instances belong in separate example ontologies; the Figure 8 tendering plan is provided in supply_chain_figure8.ttl. TaskStep and EventStep separate planned work from planned start/end milestones. CommunicationStep can describe request/reply tasks. Manufacturing-specific MakePart, AssembleProduct and DeliverProduct categories remain for a later specialization.</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_figure8/t11SendTenderForVotingTask -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_figure8/t11SendTenderForVotingTask">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Step"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/sulo/Feature"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/sulo/Object"/>
