    <!-- https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/baseModelMetadata -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/baseModelMetadata">
        <sulo:contains rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/baseModelMetadata"/>
        <sulo:hasPart rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/baseModelMetadata"/>
        <sulo:isIn rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/baseModelMetadata"/>
        <sulo:isPartOf rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/baseModelMetadata"/>
        <terms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-22</terms:created>
        <terms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8824-9577"/>
        <terms:description xml:lang="en">Self-contained experimental merge of Bro_Pro (Big_Bro/SULO, a PROV-O subset and P-Plan) with OWL-Time. Seven direct-date SWRL rules derive all thirteen Allen base relations using the retained inverse axioms; one additional SWRL rule propagates qualified PROV associations. No catalog or owl:imports resolution is required.</terms:description>
        <terms:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-22</terms:modified>
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/process_model/mergedSourceMetadata"/>
        <terms:title xml:lang="en">Process model: Bro_Pro with OWL-Time and Allen interval rules</terms:title>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Temporal rule contract: each interval needs one unambiguous beginning and end, each represented by an instant with a timezone-qualified xsd:dateTimeStamp value using time:inXSDDateTimeStamp. Rules require positive duration and complete timestamps; they do not reason over uncertain or undated endpoints. Allen equality does not imply owl:sameAs. PROV literal start/end properties alone do not supply these endpoint paths. SULO temporal quantities have not been equated with OWL-Time entities. Legacy named temporal examples are retained.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Unchanged header annotations from the corrected reusable process_model base used for this extension. The base source file is a separate deliverable.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Process model</rdfs:label>
        <owl:versionInfo>experimental-base-sync-2026-10-22</owl:versionInfo>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-10-22 review: verified the original six enabled rules against the published W3C Time With SWRL Rules V2.ttl. Retained direct endpoint comparison; changed the before head to intervalBefore; completed finishes/finishedBy; used value comparisons for equal boundaries; guarded against zero/reversed durations. Fixed the January gMonth literal. Restored Bundle-to-Entity and qualified-association typing, corrected the agent domain to AgentInfluence, and added the SWRL equivalent of the PROV association chain. Retained the original header at pm:mergedSourceMetadata. P-Plan and SULO logical axioms and existing test individuals are otherwise unchanged.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-10-22 — Changed by ChatGPT. Synchronized the reusable process_model base with the later corrections in bro_pro_corrected.ttl before creating any domain-specific extension. Restored both prov:hadRole domains: prov:Influence and the union of prov:Association with prov:InstantaneousEvent. Restored prov:EmptyCollection as an owl:Class and subclass of prov:Collection, and prov:Collection as an owl:Class and subclass of prov:Entity, retaining the existing named-individual declaration for prov:EmptyCollection. Copied the corresponding PROV labels, definitions and source annotations, including the additional annotations on AgentInfluence, Association and Bundle. Verified that the earlier association repairs, seven direct-date Allen SWRL rules, qualified-association rule and January datatype correction were already present; preserved all eight rule bodies without duplication. Retained the ontology IRI, P-Plan and SULO definitions, all existing example individuals and dates, and earlier ontology metadata. No supply-chain vocabulary, test fixtures or inferred assertions were added.</skos:changeNote>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <rdf:Description>
        <xsd:pattern>---(0[1-9]|[1-9][0-9])(Z|(\+|-)((0[0-9]|1[0-3]):[0-5][0-9]|14:00))?</xsd:pattern>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description>
        <xsd:pattern>--(0[1-9]|1[0-9]|20)(Z|(\+|-)((0[0-9]|1[0-3]):[0-5][0-9]|14:00))?</xsd:pattern>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description>
        <xsd:pattern>-?([1-9][0-9]{3,}|0[0-9]{3})(Z|(\+|-)((0[0-9]|1[0-3]):[0-5][0-9]|14:00))?</xsd:pattern>
    </rdf:Description>
    


